# moby-subtick-corpus.manifest — rows of scripts/check_moby_subtick.sh.
#   <bk2> | <lo>-<hi> | pairs=<n> class=<n> [dmax=<px>] [| leg|seam <vbl> <moby> <reason>]...
#   bk2    a movie under games/spyro-1/bk2
#   span   intermediate-capture VBLs, two apart; exclusions name the VBL the
#          [moby-anim] trace prints
# The Argus rescue in Artisans: several dragons and NPCs cross clip switches.
# Spyro 1 rebuilds both poses host-side from the state bytes, so its seam
# carries no integer-record floor and every leg reads D = 0.
# 1828: 8016fa68 (class 0x0a) switches from animation 1 (122 vertices) into
# animation 3 (16), between which no pose exists; the held leg checks that
# the present shows the 1826 pose until alpha 1.
artisans-rescue-argus.bk2 | 1714-1838 | pairs=619 class=17 hold=1 dmax=0.0005
